In article <1991Jul13.082232.25227@fs7.ece.cmu.edu> hairston@henry.ece.cmu.edu (David Hairston) writes:
> [] 6. Which class is the best to play?
> 
> hmmm, perhaps a Priest(ess) for novices.  they can read curses just
> by looking at objects.  the other classes are sufficiently different
> that you'll have to decide for yourself ...

I'd have to disagree with you on that.  Sure Priests know the cursed/blessed
status of objects, but they are weak and poorly armored and are therefore
rather hard to keep alive.  The best character for a novice to play would be
either a Barbarian or a Valkyrie.  Both of these characters are strong and well
protected and are perfect for the slash and hack strategy that most new 
players use.  
I agree that Priests and Wizards are more fun to play, however it takes
some experience to get them past the first few levels.

